       <h2 id="email">FTW news and the FTW box waitlist</h2>
       <p>On this website you can give us your email address for FTW news, for the FTW box waitlist, or both. We store the address, the list you joined, your country if you chose one, which consent you gave and when. We store nothing else from the form, and no IP address. We use the address only for that list: news about FTW, or an email when FTW boxes go on sale, with the price and shipping. We do not sell it or share it for advertising.</p>
-      <p>The legal basis is your consent. You can leave a list at any time: every email we send will have a link for it, or email <a href="mailto:support@sourceful.energy">support@sourceful.energy</a>. We then delete your address from that list. We delete the waitlist when the box sale ends. The addresses are kept in a Cloudflare D1 database in the EU that Sourceful controls; Cloudflare processes them on our behalf. Before we send the first email, we will name the service that sends it here.</p>
+      <p>The legal basis is your consent. You can leave a list at any time with the link at the bottom of every email, or by emailing <a href="mailto:support@sourceful.energy">support@sourceful.energy</a>. We then delete your address from that list. So that we do not email you again by mistake, we keep a one-way hash of it: a fingerprint we can match a new sign-up against, but cannot turn back into the address. We delete the waitlist when the box sale ends.</p>
+      <p>The addresses are kept in a Cloudflare D1 database in the EU that Sourceful controls; Cloudflare processes them on our behalf. We send the emails with Utskick, our own open source newsletter sender, and they are delivered by Amazon Simple Email Service from Amazon Web Services' Frankfurt region in Germany; Amazon Web Services processes the address and the email on our behalf. When you click a link in one of our emails, the click passes through our own server first, which records which link it was and when, and nothing about your device or IP address. FTW emails have no tracking image, so we do not record whether you opened them. If an email cannot be delivered or is reported as spam, we stop sending to that address.</p>
 
       <h2>Your rights</h2>
       <p>Sourceful Labs AB (reg. no. 559382-0458), Kalmar, Sweden, is responsible for the data FTW Cloud and the relay handle. Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, and object to how we use it. FTW Cloud holds no name, email address or street address for you, but your home id and IP addresses count as personal data. To ask, email <a href="mailto:support@sourceful.energy">support@sourceful.energy</a> or use <a href="https://www.sourceful.energy/contact">Sourceful's contact page</a>. You can also complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (<a href="https://www.imy.se/en/">IMY</a>).</p>
